(3) G9: does keying settling to the baryons' accretion history need a direct baryon-cold coupling?
====================================================================================================================
  per-parcel signal, N = 20000: the eligible boundary shell's own partner baryons (7.25e-04 M_b) vs the mass enclosed at its time-averaged radius (0.1064 r_ta0): dg/g = 6.96e-05
  per-parcel signal, N = 5000: the eligible boundary shell's own partner baryons (2.90e-03 M_b) vs the mass enclosed at its time-averaged radius (0.0607 r_ta0): dg/g = 4.67e-04
  ratio (N=5000)/(N=20000) = 6.707 (1/N scaling predicts 4.000)
  POST-HOC, same radius 0.1064 r_ta0 (time-averaged enclosed mass): dg/g = 7.33e-05 (N=20000), 3.25e-04 (N=5000), ratio 4.434: the per-parcel signal is the shell's own baryon mass over an O(1) enclosed mass, so it vanishes as 1/N in the continuum
  collective signal at r_edge (1e10, canonical, q = 0.1): if the galaxy's baryons stayed on the eligible orbits, the baryons inside r_edge drop by 0.317 M_b against 5.86 M_b enclosed: dg/g = 0.054 (O(f_b); halo-level, not per parcel)

  classification (literal rule | best gravitational surrogate):
    CS-P: G9-FAIL (needs q in Gal(t) for every cold parcel (partner identity across species)) | surrogate: cap = (rho_c/rho_b)_cosmic x M_b,gal: species-split M_b,gal and the settled cold's own enclosed mass (G9-TENSION); with the ratio read from (own density, K) it is the share cap written as a law = the edge definition
    CS-I: G9-FAIL (partner identity (as CS-P) plus inward-only motion) | surrogate: Lagrangian cut M_L(q) <= M_b,gal/f_b: M_L latched from its own turnaround field is clean, M_b,gal is species-split (G9-TENSION), f_b a coefficient; and the cut IS the R1 assumption, not retention physics
    CS-0: G9-FAIL (partner identity) | surrogate: as CS-I
    CS-M: G9-FAIL (partner identity and the galaxy's baryon mass at each accretion) | surrogate: needs M_b,gal(t) along the history: species-split (G9-TENSION) and per-shell identity (FAIL)
    CS-F: G9-FAIL (as CS-M) | surrogate: as CS-M

